course: dictionary
lesson: 6683
title: Watch closely: the word observe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To observe means to watch something carefully so that you learn about it. Scientists observe plants, the weather and the night sky. «Evidence is what you observe and measure, not what you hope or believe.» Here observe means to watch and measure carefully, not to guess.
explain: Observe can also mean to notice or see something. Look at the clues around the word. «Hawking's leaking, called Hawking radiation, has never been directly observed, because it is far too faint.» The words because it is far too faint tell you that observed means seen or detected, which is very hard when something is faint.
explain: In formal language, observe can mean to obey. «Everyone must observe the speed limit» means everyone must obey it, not watch it. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Observe goes with observation. An observation is what you see or measure, and a good scientist writes observations down carefully. When you are not sure what a word means, read the words around it first, and use a dictionary if you still need help.
fact: Observe means to watch something carefully to learn about it.
fact: «Observed» means seen or watched carefully, often by measuring or recording.
fact: An observation is what you see or measure, not what you guess or hope.
fact: In formal language, to observe a rule or law means to obey it.
fact: Phrases to remember: observe closely, observe the rules.
exercise: «Hawking radiation has never been directly observed, because it is far too faint.» What does observed mean here? | *Seen or detected by watching carefully | Taken away for ever | Painted bright red | Ignored because it is loud
exercise: Ravi must observe his plant each day and write down what he notices. What should he do? | Guess how it grows without looking | Water it once and then forget it | Pull it out to check the roots | *Watch it carefully and write down what he sees
exercise: «Evidence is what you observe and measure, not what you hope or believe.» According to this sentence, what is evidence? | What you hope | What you believe | *What you observe and measure | What your friends say
test: What does observe mean in «observe the rules»? | Shout them out | *Obey them | Write them down | Forget them
test: A scientist writes down what she sees when she observes the sky. What is an observation? | *What you see or measure | A guess about the stars | A drawing of the moon | A rule for the sky
exam: In «Hawking radiation has never been directly observed, because it is far too faint», what does this suggest about observing it? | It is easy to measure from the ground | It has been observed by every scientist | It is so bright that everyone can see it | *It is very faint, so it is hard to detect
